From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 08:53:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] PCI/pwrctrl: allow the power sequencing driver to be built in

PCI_PWRCTRL_PWRSEQ has no prompt: it is only selected by the drivers of
the devices it powers (ath11k, ath12k), so it is a module whenever they
are. A PCIe host driver that is built in then defers its probe until
the module has been loaded and bound (pci_pwrctrl_power_on_devices()
returns -EPROBE_DEFER while the pwrctrl device has no driver). On a
Qualcomm tablet with a WCN7860 the controller probes 11 times before the
initramfs loads the module, about 1.3 s into the boot.

Give the symbol a prompt, so that a configuration can build it in
together with its power sequencing provider. Its default and the
selects are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/pci/pwrctrl/Kconfig | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/pwrctrl/Kconfig b/drivers/pci/pwrctrl/Kconfig
index 9eec767cda86..df7232890dd5 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/pwrctrl/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/pci/pwrctrl/Kconfig
@@ -7,9 +7,15 @@ config PCI_PWRCTRL
 	tristate
 
 config PCI_PWRCTRL_PWRSEQ
-	tristate
+	tristate "PCI Power Control driver using the Power Sequencing subsystem"
 	select POWER_SEQUENCING
 	select PCI_PWRCTRL
+	help
+	  Power control for PCI devices whose supplies are handled by a
+	  power sequencing provider, such as the Qualcomm WCN Wi-Fi /
+	  Bluetooth packages. Drivers of such devices select it; say Y here
+	  to build it in, so that the PCIe controller does not have to wait
+	  for the module before it can power the device and train the link.
 
 config PCI_PWRCTRL_GENERIC
 	tristate "Generic PCI Power Control driver for PCI slots and endpoints"
-- 
